    <name>
      <text>intro-sequences-q1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the sequence:</p>
<p>\({@t1@}, \; {@t2@}, \; {@t3@}, \; {@t4@}, \; \ldots\)</p>
<p>The first term is \(a_1 = {@t1@}\), and the pattern continues. Find:</p>

<p>(a) The \(5^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_5\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) The \(6^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_6\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) The \(7^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_7\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) The \(10^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_{10}\).</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The sequence is {@t1@}, {@t2@}, {@t3@}, {@t4@}, ... Each term is found by adding the same number to the term before it.</p>

<p>First, find the step between terms:</p>
<p>\[ {@t2@} - {@t1@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( {@t3@} - {@t2@} = {@ta1@} \) and \( {@t4@} - {@t3@} = {@ta1@} \). The step is always the same, so each term is {@ta1@} more than the one before.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>\(5^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_5\):</strong></p>
<p>\[ a_5 = a_4 + {@d@} = {@t4@} + {@d@} = {@ta2@} \]</p>

<p>(b) <strong>\(6^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_6\):</strong></p>
<p>\[ a_6 = a_5 + {@d@} = {@ta2@} + {@d@} = {@ta3@} \]</p>

<p>(c) <strong>\(7^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_7\):</strong></p>
<p>\[ a_7 = a_6 + {@d@} = {@ta3@} + {@d@} = {@ta4@} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>\(10^{\text{th}}\) term, \(a_{10}\):</strong></p>
<p>From the \(7^{\text{th}}\) term, add {@d@} three more times to reach the \(10^{\text{th}}\) term:</p>
<p>\[ a_{10} = a_7 + 3 \times {@d@} = {@ta4@} + {@d@}\times 3 = {@ta5@} \]</p>

<p>The sequence continues: \( {@t1@}, \; {@t2@}, \; {@t3@}, \; {@t4@}, \; {@ta2@}, \; {@ta3@}, \; {@ta4@}, \; \ldots \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
